# PoW-Hook developer configuration.  Copy to .env (never commit .env).
#
# Every setting lives in ONE variable: POW, a JSON object.  Keys:
#
#   checks_cmd          The real tree scan.  MUST match "checks_cmd" in
#                       .github/workflows/pow-validator.yml byte-for-byte (the
#                       validator compares a SHA-256 of the string).  Keep the
#                       scanner image pinned.
#   corpus_cmd          Challenge-corpus scan (proof that the scanner really
#                       ran).  Same pinned image, JSON output; {corpus_dir} is
#                       replaced with the temp directory holding the corpus.
#   github_pat_local    Token used to dispatch the attestation ledger and
#                       download challenge artifacts.
#                         classic PAT:      scopes  repo, workflow
#                         fine-grained PAT: repository permission Actions: Read and write
#   github_repo         owner/repo slug (install.sh fills this in from the origin remote).
#   github_api_url      GitHub Enterprise Server API base (omit for github.com).
#   ledger_ref          Ref pow-ledger.yml is dispatched on (must equal "ledger_ref"
#                       in pow-validator.yml; default "main").
#   challenge_timeout   Seconds to wait for the minted corpus (default 180).
#   challenge_poll      Seconds between ledger polls (default 5).
#   challenge_optional  "true": fall back to a v1 trailer when minting fails
#                       (the server only accepts v1 while "allow_v1" is "true").
#   ssh_key             Path to the SSH private key registered on your GitHub
#                       account (written by setup_hooks.py).
#
# Without github_pat_local + github_repo + corpus_cmd the hooks emit v1
# trailers (no challenge receipt).
#
# Example with the pinned trufflehog scanner (add github_pat_local / github_repo):
POW='{"checks_cmd":"docker run --rm -v \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\":/pwd trufflesecurity/trufflehog:3.99.8 filesystem /pwd --no-verification --fail","corpus_cmd":"docker run --rm -v \"{corpus_dir}\":/pwd trufflesecurity/trufflehog:3.99.8 filesystem /pwd --no-verification --json"}'
